      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">~20 Dogs, Every Single Night</h2>
      <div class="text-sm md:text-base text-secondary leading-relaxed space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
        <p>There's no emergency here. No rush to the vet. No dramatic rescue. This is the quiet, unglamorous, repetitive work that actually keeps animals alive — and it happens every single night.</p>
        <p>Since 2025, I've been feeding and looking after the wellness of around 20 community dogs in a small pocket of North Bangalore. Every night without exception. Rain, travel, deadlines, exhaustion — none of it matters. They're waiting regardless, and they don't understand the concept of a day off.</p>
        <p>A dog that eats regularly doesn't fight for scraps. A dog that sees the same person every night stops flinching when humans walk by. That quiet shift — from fear to recognition to trust — is the entire point. It won't make headlines, but it's the most meaningful thing I do.</p>
